    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i hear that, but you're being kind of vague. like, if you look at cases like Bruen, the court basically said regulations have to be consistent with historical tradition. doesn't that pretty much invalidate the \"public safety\" argument if there isn't a historical precedent for it? it feels like the legal window for strict control has basically slammed shut.",
