    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "so if the current legal framework \"heavily favors\" one side, isn't it basically just admitting that the old way of doing things—where the gov could just pass laws for public safety—is effectively dead? it seems like the court has basically decided that historical precedent is more important than modern reality. don't you think that's a pretty clear-cut shift in what's considered \"legitimate\" law?",
